.TH MD_PROCESS_SPECTRUM 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_process_spectrum \- feed one calibrated linear-power spectrum frame
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

int md_process_spectrum(morsedec_decoder_t *decoder, const float
    *power, size_t count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Feed one calibrated linear-power spectrum frame.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.TP
.I power
Non-NULL array containing linear power, in ascending retained-bin order.
Borrowed during the call.
.TP
.I count
Exactly geometry.spectrum_size float values. One call advances one complete
hop.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns MORSEDEC_SUCCESS (1) on success, or MORSEDEC_FAILURE (0) and sets
errno on failure. Do not inspect errno after success.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
NULL decoder or power, wrong count, sample-input mode selected, or input after
flush.
.SH REMARKS
Available on both audio and I/Q handles. Geometry must match
md_get_geometry(): bin j is first_frequency+j*bin_spacing and successive calls
represent frame_seconds apart. I/Q bins include negative offsets, ascending
through zero; they are not in raw FFT output order. NaN, infinite, zero and
negative powers become zero.
.PP
The first call selects external-spectrum mode. Audio or I/Q sample calls then
fail until md_reset(); spectrum input likewise fails after sample mode is
selected. md_flush() seals this mode too. Processing performs no allocation,
blocking I/O or callbacks.
.PP
Frames must match the frontend window and power calibration, not merely its
bin count. The FFT is unnormalized. For N=fft_size, fs=sample_rate and
i=0..N-1, use:
.nf
a = 2*pi*25*(i-N/2)/fs
w[i] = (0.42-0.5*cos(2*pi*i/N)+0.08*cos(4*pi*i/N))
       * sinc(a) * (8000/fs)
sinc(a) = sin(a)/a; sinc(0) = 1
audio power = 0.001 * abs(FFT(w*x))^2
I/Q power   = 0.00025 * abs(FFT(w*(I+jQ)))^2
.fi
.PP
Preserve sample-window alignment and the same temporal response. A generic SDR
waterfall in dB, a different window, or a differently normalized FFT is not a
compatible input. The one-quarter I/Q power coefficient compensates for the
doubled amplitude of an isolated complex exponential relative to a real
sinusoid of equal peak amplitude.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0.
Version 0.3.0 uses the float API and shared-library ABI 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
